<title>LITHUANIA: UTENOS SHARE CAPITAL REGISTERED.</title>
<headline>UTENOS SHARE CAPITAL REGISTERED.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's securities commission said on Monday it had registered Utena Beverages 22.8 million litas share issue following the settlement of a long-running dispute over the state's stake in the company.</p>
<p>&quot;It's the first time that they've been registered with the commission,&quot; Dalius Simenas, a spokesman for the securities commission, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Shareholders in Utena, which is 21.5-percent state-owned, decided on July 21 to form a closed joint stock company with Baltic Beverage Holdings (BBH). BBH is owned by Finnish Hartwall and Norway's Orkla , .</p>
<p>The decision was a rejection for Denmark's Carlsberg, which had also been courting Utena.</p>
<p>Utenos was Lithuania's top brewer, in terms of production and sales, in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Burton Frierson, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 18</p>
